# GP1-VIEWMODES (GP1 p8): the editor's view mode (Wireframe, World Normal) is the VIEWPORT's state and reaches the Play view by the same path as the edit view (UE: the PIE viewport inherits EViewModeIndex/ShowFlags).
# Mirage's MainMenu is only a test scene (owner 10-30): its look is not judged here, only that each mode shows.
Проект ../Mirage/Mirage.deproj
Дано run Scene "Open Scene MainMenu.desce"
Дано run View "View mode: Wireframe"
Тогда-вид edit_wireframe reference, edit view without Play: wireframe lines over a dark background
Когда run View "View mode: World Normal"
Тогда-вид edit_worldnormal reference, edit view without Play: coloured world normals, not black
Когда run View "View mode: Lit"
Когда run Action "Play from Here"
Когда advance 1
Когда run View "View mode: Wireframe"
Когда advance 0.3
Тогда-вид play_wireframe Play view: the landscape's wireframe mesh over a dark background, not the lit frame
Когда run View "View mode: World Normal"
Когда advance 0.3
Тогда-вид play_worldnormal Play view: coloured world normals of the dunes, not a black frame
Когда run View "View mode: Lit"
Когда advance 0.3
Тогда-вид play_lit Play view: the ordinary lit menu background, as before the switches
